    "What is your relationship with mathematics?": "I’ve always had a mix of respect and dread about math—my parents pushed me hard when I was younger, especially since my father struggled with it too. Now, though, physics fascinates me, but algebra feels like an intimidating barrier. It’s not that I fear failure, but the abstract steps sometimes leave me stuck. My approach now is to focus on problem-solving instead of memorization, and I rely more on visualizing equations than formulas.",
